// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// T27 OS native_accept (v0.1.0-alpha.1): the acceptance suite of the native foundation line. Six groups, A to F,
// named in the order of the brief. Run it with
//
//     t27b test specs/t27os/native_accept.t27
//
// A test passes only if it ran and its assertions held. Which tests need what:
//   - the LM Studio tests (b_*, c_live_*, d_one_agent_*, e_three_agents_*) need a server on 127.0.0.1:1234. The
//     environment is optional: T27OS_LMSTUDIO_HOST, _PORT, _MODEL and _API_KEY override the defaults, and a
//     missing model is taken from the first one the server lists. Each of them asserts the endpoint loads
//     first, so with no server they FAIL; they never pass on a mock and never skip silently.
//   - every other test needs nothing but a writable target/ directory.
//
// Files go to target/t27os/native-accept (gitignored). Session, agent and swarm ids come from the clock
// (fresh_base), so a rerun never meets an old log; the one fixed id is 8102 in c_a_session_file_outlives_*,
// which appends three events per run on purpose and so proves, from the second run on, that a file written
// by an earlier process reads back whole. Delete the directory to reset it.
//
// The restart of acceptance C is a reload from the file: every in-memory copy is dropped and the session is
// rebuilt from the bytes on disk by native_log. A separate process restart is only covered by running the suite
// twice (c_a_session_file_outlives_* reads what the first run left).
//
// DSH is not imported anywhere in the native line, so no test here can need it.
//
// Refs gHashTag/t27#13212.
